{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>I will do as you say.</b> Midrash: just as you command me, so I command my brothers at the time of my death to bring me up from here. And so we find that he said to his brothers: ״פקוד יפקד אלהים אתכם״ etc. And it appears to us that from this it is resolved — that which Rashi explained in the beginning of Exodus, that this sign was handed down to them from Jacob and from Joseph: that through this expression of פקוד יפקד they will be redeemed, for we find that Joseph said explicitly ״פקוד יפקד אלהים אתכם״, and he said here that Joseph said he would do as the words of Jacob. And if so, Jacob too said in his testament ״פקוד יפקד אלהים אתכם״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {0 "The text quotes both פקוד יפקד and פקד יפקד; both forms retained as they appear."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:15.766580541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}